        "caseheaddatetime": "2023-08-11T15:38:00.000Z",
        "childdescription": "Zion said he was being carried by his father during the argument that is the subject of this report. Zion is an average to large size 8.5 year old. He was not injured.  Neither he nor Canyon disclosed anything physical, just that there was yelling and mean words between the parents. Children both stated they feel safe with both parents but get nervous when their parents yell. Zion said he had just been struck by Canyon and the parents were working on that situation. Father said he was taking Zion to watch TV. Mother wanted him to go to bed. Father said there is a protective order as a result of the incident and will email a copy.",
        "childRelationship": null,
        "caregiverdescription": "Father stated that he went to Florida for a month on military orders and came back 11:30pm June 1 to friends house, then home on June 2, he went to the family home and was \"appalled at condition of home\".  He said he had pictures of 3 bags of clothes along a wall in the master bedroom as well as pictures of the kids'' rooms with a few toys and clothes on their beds. He said the cat liter box not cleaned for days.  As the couple sleeps separately, he said her room was not cleaned for months, and he found \"jars of [prescription] narcotics\" in her room.\nShe has accused him of stalking.\n\nOn the night that prompted this report, the kids were fighting, he wanted to separate the kids - older kid fought with younger brother. She did not like that he was taking Zion downstairs to watch TV when he should be going to bed.\n\nHe said she had walked to the mailbox at the end of their long driveway and left the kids in the house.  Lawyers do not want them to contact her, she says she is fearful of him but she puts her hand on him.  They have been married 9 years.  They lived in the current family home since Dec 2021 and before that was in middle east for 3 years.\n\nMother works as Transitional Assistant for CCPS. Father is a crewman in the Navy and is not working currently. He has a \"high-level clearance\".  Children in therapy on base - Dad had to engage because mom said it too inconvenient.",
        "caregiverrelationship": null
    },
