        "referralsource": "Agency perception is that the family has experienced crisis as a result of the recent separation and one or both parents are focused on hurting the other and not seeing the effect on the children. Case was referred to on-going consolidated services. ",
        "timeCompletion": "45 days",
        "caseheaddatetime": "2023-09-29T16:06:00.000Z",
        "childdescription": "In the initial investigation, Zion said he was being carried by his father during the argument that is the subject of the report. Zion is an average to large size 8.5 year old. He was not injured.  Neither he nor Canyon disclosed anything physical, just that there was yelling and mean words between the parents. Children both stated they feel safe with both parents but get nervous when their parents yell. Zion said he had just been struck by Canyon and the parents were working on that situation. Father said he was taking Zion to watch TV. Mother wanted him to go to bed. Zion and Canyon have not been re-questioned about this incident but display behaviors that are consistent with the trauma of their parents ongoing conflict. ",
        "childRelationship": null,
        "caregiverdescription": "During the initial investigation Mr. Aarons stated that he went to Florida for a month on military orders and came back 11:30pm June 1 to friends house, then home on June 2, he went to the family home and was \"appalled at condition of home\".  He said he had pictures of 3 bags of clothes along a wall in the master bedroom as well as pictures of the kids'' rooms with a few toys and clothes on their beds. He said the cat liter box not cleaned for days.  As the couple sleeps separately, he said her room was not cleaned for months, and he found \"jars of [prescription] narcotics\" in her room.  Ms. Aarons accused him of stalking her. \n\nOn the night that prompted this report, the kids were fighting, Mr. Aarons reported that he wanted to separate the kids - older kid fought with younger brother. Ms. Aarons did not like that he was taking Zion downstairs to watch TV when he should be going to bed. Mr. Aarons reported that this argument resulted in her grabbing at him and almost causing him to fall down the stairs while carrying Zion. He reported that she had also walked to the mailbox at the end of their long driveway and left the kids in the house unattended.  Ms. Aarons claims she is fearful of him but she puts her hands on him.  They have been married 9 years.  They lived in the current family home since Dec 2021 and before that was in middle east for 3 years.\n\nMother works as Transitional Assistant for CCPS. Father is a crewman in the Navy and is not working currently. He has a \"high-level clearance\".  Children were enrolled in crisis intervention therapy on base following a Fleet and Family investigation. Dad had to engage because mom said it was too inconvenient.\nCurrently both parents report concerns about each other''s parenting methods. Mr. Aarons continues to allege neglect due to home conditions and allowing the boys to be physical with her as well as engaging in physical disputes in their presence and leaving prescription medications accessible to them. Ms. Aarons alleges that Mr. Aarons is abusive and controlling towards both herself and the boys. She alleges that he uses physical punishment with the boys and speaks poorly about her around them, which has resulted in them treating her poorly. She feels that mental abuse is the primary issue. Both parents want full custody granted to them and report difficulties with co-parenting. ",
        "caregiverrelationship": null
    },
